{"recordedAt":"2026-11-24T15:37:16.037Z","repo":"lhpaul/ronda","pullNumber":117,"stage":"plan","headSha":"194f66e5f3d469bc897e78ce4058c4883fa93ca0","arm":"C","run":2,"modelRequested":"deepseek-v4-pro-0813","temperature":0,"checklistSha256":"9c3de62d1f51d4b1709888f4c7a28766cf4afde079a26dd5107b778a59a56cde","dryRun":false,"patchSource":"synthesize","filesWithoutGithubPatch":[],"excludedFiles":[],"inputSha256":"f42374b27526c230f53f34ca4c66ac717a778590c29b3aafda4134a63ea20ece","manifestSha256":"f7fd1ab0bc1b793f37b06dc11ae229ce5137c0eeba01056c0b9a5c3285b869d1","promptSha256":"fe7b47162f45ebb545b8ac9f91e1092baa9e02b1c14ef56c0c9ec0e28b305f45","findingCount":7,"findings":[{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":1,"severity":"important","title":"PR description is missing the Document Quality Gate log","body":"The PR description is empty, but plan PRs must include a current Document Quality Gate log. This plan contains a stateful Decision-gate matrix, so the log would also need the Matrix coherence preflight row with the six-check audit summary. Without the log, coverage claims cannot be checked and the matrix audit record is absent."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":1,"severity":"blocking","title":"Plan authoring rigor outcome record and required six-rule block are absent","body":"The plan has no Plan authoring rigor section naming Rule 1 through Rule 6 by canonical names, no per-rule outcome labels (Satisfied/Not applicable/Unsatisfied), and no link to plan-authoring-rigor-rules.md. The review checklist treats a missing outcome record as blocking and requires the six-rule block for mirror-harness assertions. Add the required block and per-rule outcomes rather than relying on the Verification Log."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":68,"severity":"blocking","title":"Sweep prompt requirement leaks category identifiers into the published review body","body":"The review-prompt change instructs the model that a swept-category finding 'must name that category's identifier in its own title or body text'. That makes the review body contain sweep-specific identifier text a non-sweep pass would not emit, conflicting with the spec's 'Findings themselves are published exactly as in a non-sweep review' and with AC1's separation of per-category records from the review body. The plan's assertion that this 'changes no part of the output contract' only covers field shape, not the published content. Classify against the raw finding text using the recorded match terms/identifiers without requiring the model to inject identifiers, or explicitly revise the plan to justify the new observable review-body behavior."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":111,"severity":"blocking","title":"Concurrency addendum contradicts the planned timer/abort-controller change","body":"The Concurrent-event-source addendum says the sweep 'adds no listener, timer, or async queue' and 'deadline/teardown machinery is unchanged', but Implementation Order step 11 moves the AbortController/passTimeoutMs timer inside each `--runs` iteration and creates/disposes one per run. That is a direct cross-section contradiction, and the addendum's Not applicable classification skips the required concurrency-safety checklist. Either keep the current single timer or classify the addendum as applicable and address the seven checklist items for the new per-run timer/abort lifecycle."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":140,"severity":"important","title":"Seed Data step reference points at the wrong implementation step","body":"The Original-thirteen fixture snapshot row says the copy happens 'before step 9 mutates the live fixture', but step 9 is the workflow/example-config change and does not mutate the fixture; the live fixture is mutated in step 10 (Fixture seeds). This cross-reference is stale and will mislead the implementer about ordering. Update it to reference step 10."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":196,"severity":"important","title":"Benchmark driver section cites the evidence document as step 11 instead of step 12","body":"Implementation Order step 11 ends with 'The evidence doc (step 11) is assembled from those files', but the evidence document is written in step 12 (Evidence campaign). Step 11 only builds the benchmark driver. Correct the cross-reference so the implementation sequence is unambiguous."},{"path":"docs/specs/developments/20260925143028_105-category-forced-review-sweep/2_105-category-forced-review-sweep_implementation-plan.md","line":134,"severity":"important","title":"New seed patch paths are specified as 'or similar' rather than concrete paths","body":"Every new seed in the Seed Data table names a path such as `src/benchmark/git-history.ts` followed by 'or similar'. The implementation step then depends on the developer choosing the actual patch target, which leaves the AC12/AC13 fixture work guessable. Either pin each seed to a verified concrete patch path or record that the path is illustrative and add a step to choose/verify it before implementation."}],"malformedCount":0,"promptChars":256706,"responseChars":5021,"elapsedMs":760055,"outcome":"findings","modelReported":"deepseek-v4-pro-0813"}
